816	    /// base value back anyway, leaving a control that reported success and
817	    /// did nothing. A `text` object naming `words` is an `Err` too (format
818	    /// version 9, spec §11 W-6): a word's times are anchored to speech, not
819	    /// a state a clip ramps toward, and interpolating two lists of ticks
820	    /// would move every word off what it times. A `video.cutout` naming
821	    /// `subject` or `quality`, a `null` included, is an `Err` as well
822	    /// ([`check_cutout_end`], spec §11 CO-20): both are the clip's base.
